  "dependency": "DUB-17 frozen Theorem 2.6 / DUB-18 Corollary 8.2 -> symmetric-power continuation -> arithmetic automorphy -> residual Galois association -> original parabolic Hecke realization -> period surjectivity -> matching cusp-form lower dimension bound -> regular differential dimension -> Riemann--Roch -> actual original curve: principal-divisor finite support and degree zero, finite residues, and differential rank one.",
  "discharged": "For the actual original modular function field, the proved finite extension over the original j coordinate gives a one-dimensional differential space. The literal Euler-derivative kernel gives exactly the base constants. Every actual place uniformizer has order one while constants have order zero, so its differential is nonzero and spans. Thus regularity is equivalent to integrality of the actual local differential coefficient at every place. Q-expansion of the actual regular differential subspace is injective. No local spanning or separability premise remains. The actual original divisor-generated field is essentially of finite type. It is finite over every transcendental coordinate, in particular every actual place uniformizer. Actual regularity equals nonnegative local differential order. Every actual place residue is algebraic over the base: a transcendental residue would put its lifted rational function field, and hence the entire finite extension, in a proper integrally closed valuation ring. Over algebraically closed constants the actual residue map is bijective and the residue is finite. No finite-residue, finite-coordinate or local-spanning premise remains on these consumers. Every function in the actual original modular function field has only finitely many nonzero normalized place orders. For a transcendental function the proved finite coordinate extension gives a Dedekind integral-closure chart. Actual places containing the chart are identified with their actual prime centers. Pinned finiteness of prime ideal factors bounds the positive support; inversion handles negative support. Algebraic functions have order zero at every actual place. No finite-support or place-classification premise remains. Every actual original-field function has a finite normalized-order divisor with degree zero. The actual chart primes and positive-order places correspond bijectively; their normalized orders equal pinned ramification indices, and their residue degrees equal pinned inertia degrees. The pinned ramification/inertia sum gives the degree of the positive divisor. Applying this to the function and its inverse proves degree zero, since both generate the same rational subfield. The integral-closure chart discharges all chart containment, module-finiteness, normalization and scalar-comparison inputs. Over algebraically closed constants the original curve interface is fully derived from these principal divisors, proved finite residues and proved differential rank one; no curve or principal-divisor premise remains.",
  "boundary": "Canonical divisors, Riemann--Roch, regular differential dimension, geometric genus and analytic cusp-form realization remain required for the matching lower dimension bound. Period surjectivity, Hecke/Galois realization, the adic system and symmetric-power continuation remain open. DUB-17--20 OPEN; 16/20.",
